    <innerclass refid="classhorus__generator__pattern_1_1Pattern" prot="public">horus_generator_pattern::Pattern</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacehorus__generator__pattern">horus_generator_pattern</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>YAML-driven Generator plugin, periodic waveforms with no code. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>One cycle is played at a cadence set by cycle_time, scaled by speed_factor, and shared by every signal. Each signal (joint) has its own waveform, custom table and phase offset, so a gait is expressed purely as configuration.</para>
<para>Output is ordered like the <computeroutput>signals</computeroutput> list, which must match the target controller&apos;s joints, and is written directly in the controller&apos;s units. With no <computeroutput>signals</computeroutput> list a single signal is read from the top-level parameters.</para>
<para><computeroutput>speed_factor</computeroutput> is a MULTIPLIER on the cadence rather than an absolute speed, following MARCH, whose gait phases scale a base step size the same way. 2.0 plays the cycle twice as fast.</para>
<para><computeroutput>cycling</computeroutput> decides how the behavior ENDS. A non-cycling pattern plays its cycle once and reports finished(), which is what lets a behavior action succeed (home / sit / stand); this mirrors MARCH, where a phase ends when its plan is exhausted rather than when a timer expires. A cycling pattern (a gait) never finishes on its own and runs until the behavior tree cancels it. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
